node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# `npm pack` writes the tarball into the working directory.
*.tgz

# Runtime output from the CLI. Locks and the pricing cache live under
# ~/.turnlens/, so this is the only path the tool writes inside a project.
turnlens-usage/

# docs/ is committed. It is how the tool is reasoned about, and an agent asked to
# change the code is pointed at it, so it has to exist for whoever holds the
# repository. Git also dates every document for free, which is why no document
# carries a hand-written "last updated" line.
#
# Three directories under docs/ stay behind. superpowers/ is design scaffolding
# for work in progress, work-notes/ is thinking rather than a document, and
# archive/ holds a superseded implementation kept for reference. None of them is
# something a reader of the repository needs. .local/ is for files that are not
# documents and have no other obvious home.
docs/superpowers/
docs/work-notes/
docs/archive/
.local/

# Instructions for the agent used to develop this are committed: AGENTS.md holds
# them, and CLAUDE.md is a symlink to it, because Claude Code reads that name
# while other agents read the first. `.claude/` is committed for the same reason
# -- it is written by hand. Only the permissions file Claude Code writes for
# itself stays on the machine it was written on.
.claude/settings.local.json
